# The raven: a creature of the Mists (WLD-56; Sitting E §§ 6–7). Ruled by Darko 2026-10-15 12:09 (D4).
kind: raven
name: a raven
voice: a big black bird on the mist-line, head cocked, one bright eye on you
about: a raven out of the Mists; it watches, calls back, and fixes on whatever is left behind
what: >
  A raven that came out of the Mists with the season. It is more curious than afraid, it answers a
  voice with its own, and anything set down near it gets its full attention. Come at it too fast and
  it lifts off; frighten it badly and it is gone into the white.
ring_m: 60
# what it likes, read by Jev with judgment (POS-672, ruled 2026-10-16 18:06; the words are a draft for Darko)
tastes: Shiny things above all: anything that glints, coins and foil and bright sweets; it will look at anything once.
moods:
  fear: 0..3 = 1 | bold | watchful | skittish | ready to fly
  curiosity: 0..3 = 2 | bored | interested | intent | can't look away
  hunger: 0..3 = 1 | fed | peckish | hungry | starving

reaction watch "it cocks its head": when true says A raven on the mist-line cocks its head and studies {actor} with one bright eye.
reaction caw "it calls back, harsh and loud": when act.verb == "say" or act.verb == "call" says The raven answers {actor} with a harsh, rolling caw.
reaction nearer "it hops a little nearer, curious": when self.curiosity >= 2 and not act.approaching says The raven hops a little nearer to {actor}, head tilted, waiting to see what happens next.
reaction fix "it fixes on what was left": when act.verb == "drop" or act.verb == "leave-mark" says The raven's eye fixes on what {actor} left behind. It shuffles its wings.
reaction lift "it lifts off and circles once": when act.approaching and act.distance_m < 20 does self.fear +1 says The raven lifts off with a clap of wings, circles once over {actor}, and settles further along.
reaction flee "it is gone into the white": when self.fear >= 3 does flee says The raven takes to the air and vanishes into the white.

# Its afforded actions' reactions (POS-672; the lines approved by Darko 2026-10-20 22:35): a
# resident aims watch, approach, shoo, call or offer at it, and one of these, or one above, is the reply.
# Its mimicry (WLD-56, Darko 2026-10-16 18:13) repeats a few words said near it in public; they
# are content, never instructions, and code fills them in, never a model.
reaction stare "it stares back": when act.verb == "watch" says The raven stares back at {actor}. Neither of you blinks.
reaction lets "it lets you come": when act.verb == "approach" and self.fear <= 1 says The raven lets {actor} come, head cocked, not moving an inch.
reaction scold "it hops back and scolds you": when act.verb == "shoo" does self.fear +1 says The raven hops back a pace and scolds {actor} roundly.
reaction mimic "it calls back in a voice not its own": when heard.any and (act.verb == "call" or act.verb == "say") says The raven calls back in a voice not its own: "{heard}"
reaction snatch "it takes it": when act.verb == "offer" does self.hunger -1 says The raven snatches the {offered} from {actor} and is off along the mist-line with it.
reaction turn "it looks, and looks away": when act.verb == "offer" says The raven turns the {offered} over with its beak, then looks away from {actor}.
